{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193715-the-howling-white-question","id":1193715,"title":"The \"howling white\" question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-09T15:01:18-08:00","id":1193715,"title":"The \"howling white\" question","content":"I know the whole &quot; white howlers are dead for a reason&quot; story, but still, I feel unconvinced by White wolfs book that they are trully, well dead.Because he left us, as anything to possibly chose them, tho be it if we were to play a game set before the fall of western roman empire, there is at least in my oppinion, that unsung wolf who just wasn't worth mentioning but existed as a white howler, it's a long stretch but i like to think that the end isn't nigh until it's all gone, if the Lion totem didn't fall, nor did the legacy of the howlers.But i'm sure there are great arguements to why they can't possibly be alive ( this isn't sarcasam) but there has got to be that &quot;game theory&quot; that they are still alive, just hiding, or worse, ashamed of what happened, so ashamed they can't face the garou nation anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T16:41:58-08:00","id":1193740,"title":"","content":"The White Howlers don't exist as a Tribe, even if members of the Tribe didn't fall, and have maintained their bloodline since then.<br /> <br /> You can't join a Tribe without a Tribal Totem. If the Tribal Totem refuses to allow the initiation rite to work, nobody can join the Tribe no matter what. As well, this means the Pure Breed of any surviving White Howler descendants would fail to reach spiritual potency, since that is also something the Totem powers in the Tribe's Garou.<br /> <br /> So the problem is that even if some survived, they have no way of continuing themselves as White Howlers. They would have to become Ronin, or join other Tribes (most likely the Fianna). Their culture and society is so thoroughly destroyed that they can't be said to exist in a meaningful sense, even if their are kin and Garou running around that have White Howler ancestry.<br /> <br /> For a real life comparison, there are no living Aztecs. It's not that all the Aztec people were killed off, but the Aztec culture was destroyed, and the Aztec people that survived have become part of other cultural groups (both contemporary ones, and new ones built by the mixing of Mesoamerican and Spanish cultures)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T07:23:53-08:00","id":1193918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193715-the-howling-white-question?p=1193740#post1193740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a real life comparison, there are no living Aztecs. It's not that all the Aztec people were killed off, but the Aztec culture was destroyed, and the Aztec people that survived have become part of other cultural groups (both contemporary ones, and new ones built by the mixing of Mesoamerican and Spanish cultures)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's actually plenty of Nahuatl speaking people that are still around, who practice a continuation of their culture. If you're referring to the society of the empire itself, than yes, but they're far from simply people who are descended from Aztec/Nahua people. To give you an example, Spanish speakers were only a plurality until the middle of the 19th century in Mexico. So not the best example.<br /> <br /> A better one would be the actual Picts the White Howlers were of. Sure the modern Scottish people probably overflow with Pict ancestry, but the language and very identity itself as a distinct people is gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T09:00:55-08:00","id":1193937,"title":"","content":"Well, can I at least be a Ronin who was a descendant of the white howlers, i'm mostly asking because of the gifts they had.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23861-phantomdragenoid","name":"PhantomDragenoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T09:17:59-08:00","id":1193943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhantomDragenoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193715-the-howling-white-question?p=1193937#post1193937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, can I at least be a Ronin who was a descendant of the white howlers, i'm mostly asking because of the gifts they had.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a rules for being a throwback White Howler descendant in the 2nd Edition Players Guide. I imagine they exist in W20 too. From what I recall you need to have purebreed 5, and either escape from the BSDs before they make you walk the Black Spiral (or simply sacrifice the pup) or basically be a Lunatic. The Fianna, and to a lesser extant the British Fenrir and Silver Fangs, probably took in the untainted survivors and kinfolk, so I imagine you could have a throwback born among them too. The Fianna would in particular have the possibility of possessing some knowledge of their old gifts, similar to how the Uktena and Wendigo might have knowledge of Croatan gifts.<br /> <br /> A big part of the stigma is the special snowflake syndrome and cliche of being 'the last White Howler'. If you just want to use the gifts, there's always finding a teacher from the above mentioned tribes. Because just being descended from them is not a guarantee you'd receive the gifts anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 03-10-2018, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T09:55:45-08:00","id":1193954,"title":"","content":"Also, to get a Howler throwback, yyou have too deal with centuries of inbreeding, Wyrm taint, genetic oddities and what not. Your Howler cub won't be the paragon of any sanity. Not to mention, by W20 rules, they lose their purebreed if they join any other tribe than BSDs.<br /> <br /> Even if they do, they have a -huge- target on their heads by the Dancers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T12:32:15-08:00","id":1194007,"title":"","content":"There are Lone Survivors of the the Lost Tribes. But none seem to be able to gather a Pack and without the strength of a Pack, they cannot gain territory, without territory no Kinfolk, without Kinfolk they cannot regrow their Tribe. The White Howlers need to fight to many enemies: BSD, the Fera, and the Garou of Gaia. Even if a Pack of White Howlers were gathered and rededicated to Gaia who among the Garou Nation is going to offer them territory, Kinfolk and Caerns. Unlike the Croatan and Bunyip, the White Howlers' Caern would be attacked even by the Children of Wyvern would be hard pressed to leave a sacred site in the hands of those with ties too close to the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7258-black-ushkar","name":"Black Ushkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T00:00:22-08:00","id":1194157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhantomDragenoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193715-the-howling-white-question?p=1193937#post1193937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, can I at least be a Ronin who was a descendant of the white howlers, i'm mostly asking because of the gifts they had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you can just ask your St &quot;Hey can I play a White Howler in Modern times I like their gifts&quot; or &quot;Hey could I somehow get these gifts while Play someone related to them as all the spirits still exist&quot; I mean hell you could learn all of them handed down from a Bastet with Swipe if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T05:10:41-07:00","id":1194214,"title":"","content":"It's also worth nothing that Gifts aren't exclusive unless specified. The biggest impediment towards learning a Gift is finding out it exists, because once you know it exists you just need the right kind of spirit to teach it to you (plus a way to access an appropriate spirit as detailed in the books and all). The extra effort in learning about and getting help with the spirits for non-favored Gifts is built into the extra XP costs. Any Garou can learn the Gifts in the White Howler Tribebook if the ST rules they can learn about any of the Gifts in question enough to know how to petition the appropriate spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T10:20:21-07:00","id":1194284,"title":"","content":"In W20 there are White Howler spirits in the Dark Umbra (not really a fan, but hey its cannon). You could ask your ST to have an arch involving going there and working with/befrending them so you can learn about/learn the gifts as well.<br /> <br /> Also years back I ran &quot;Past Lives&quot;, and made it so the group was able to preserve a white howler ancestor spirit who was alive and an npc during 1 of the chapters of the arc. For fun I let my players learn White Howler, Bunyip, and Croatan gifts, and be treated as those tribes for the purposes of the gifts effects. They had fun getting to play with them. Didn't bring the tribes back, but let them have this connection with those tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 03-11-2018, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T10:42:00-07:00","id":1194297,"title":"","content":"it gives 3 ways in white howler tribe book to revive tribe you can in your game if you want, but keep in mine its done only by storyteller Fiat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}